{
  "cells": [
    {
      "id": "cell_1",
      "source": "/// # Nuclear Reactor \u2014 2D Neutron Diffusion with Delayed Neutrons\n///\n/// Simulates a 2D horizontal cross-section through a thermal reactor core,\n/// solving the coupled one-group neutron diffusion and six-group delayed\n/// precursor equations on a circular geometry.\n///\n/// Periodic reactivity insertions drive the system between subcritical and\n/// delayed-supercritical states, making the interplay between **prompt** and\n/// **delayed** neutrons visible in real time.\n///\n/// ## Equations\n///\n/// From Stacey, *Nuclear Reactor Physics* (2nd ed., Wiley, 2007), Ch. 5;\n/// Keepin, *Physics of Nuclear Kinetics* (Addison-Wesley, 1965); and\n/// Lamarsh & Baratta, *Introduction to Nuclear Engineering* (3rd ed.).\n///\n/// **One-group neutron diffusion** (Stacey Eq. 5.1, simplified):\n///\n///   `(1/v) \u2202\u03c6/\u2202t = D \u2207\u00b2\u03c6 \u2212 \u03a3\u2090 \u03c6 + (1 \u2212 \u03b2) \u03bd \u03a3_f \u03c6 + \u03a3\u1d62 \u03bb\u1d62 C\u1d62 + S_ext`\n///\n/// **Delayed neutron precursor concentrations** (Keepin Ch. 4):\n///\n///   `\u2202C\u1d62/\u2202t = \u03b2\u1d62 \u03bd \u03a3_f \u03c6 \u2212 \u03bb\u1d62 C\u1d62`   for i = 1, \u2026, 6\n///\n/// where:\n///   - \u03c6(x,y,t)  = scalar neutron flux [n/cm\u00b2/s]\n///   - C\u1d62(x,y,t) = precursor concentration for group i\n///   - D          = neutron diffusion coefficient [cm]\n///   - \u03a3\u2090         = macroscopic absorption cross section [cm\u207b\u00b9]\n///   - \u03bd \u03a3_f      = neutrons per fission \u00d7 fission cross section [cm\u207b\u00b9]\n///   - \u03b2          = total delayed neutron fraction (\u03a3 \u03b2\u1d62)\n///   - \u03b2\u1d62, \u03bb\u1d62    = Keepin six-group parameters for \u00b2\u00b3\u2075U thermal fission\n///   - v          = neutron velocity [cm/s]\n///   - S_ext      = external neutron source\n///\n/// ## Visualization\n///\n/// - **Red/orange glow** = prompt fission neutron source `(1\u2212\u03b2) \u03bd \u03a3_f \u03c6`.\n///   Responds nearly instantly to reactivity changes.\n/// - **Blue/cyan glow** = delayed neutron source `\u03a3 \u03bb\u1d62 C\u1d62`.\n///   Lags behind \u2014 you can *see* the delayed neutrons sustaining flux\n///   after the prompt source drops. This is the reactor \"pulse\".\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Grid and canvas \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n/// Simulation grid resolution (N \u00d7 N cells, each cell \u2261 1 cm).\nconst N: usize = 200;\n/// Output canvas size in pixels (2\u00d7 upscale from grid).\nconst CANVAS_W: u32 = 400;\nconst CANVAS_H: u32 = 400;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Geometry \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// A circular fuel core surrounded by a reflector annulus, representing a\n// horizontal mid-plane slice through a cylindrical reactor.\n\nconst CENTER: f64 = N as f64 / 2.0;\n/// Fuel region radius [cm]. Contains fissile material (enriched UO\u2082).\nconst R_CORE: f64 = 70.0;\n/// Reflector outer radius [cm]. Water reflector, no fission.\nconst R_REFL: f64 = 90.0;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Six-group delayed neutron parameters (Keepin, 1965) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n//\n// Standard reference values for thermal fission of \u00b2\u00b3\u2075U.\n// Source: Keepin, G. R., \"Physics of Nuclear Kinetics\", Table 4-5.\n// Cross-referenced with: Lamarsh & Baratta, Table 4.2.\n//\n//   Group |   \u03b2\u1d62      |  \u03bb\u1d62 [s\u207b\u00b9] | Mean life 1/\u03bb\u1d62 [s]\n//   \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500|\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500|\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500|\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n//     1   | 0.000215  |  0.0124   |  80.6  (longest-lived)\n//     2   | 0.001424  |  0.0305   |  32.8\n//     3   | 0.001274  |  0.111    |   9.0\n//     4   | 0.002568  |  0.301    |   3.3  (largest \u03b2 fraction)\n//     5   | 0.000748  |  1.14     |   0.88\n//     6   | 0.000273  |  3.01     |   0.33 (shortest-lived)\n//\n// \u03b2_total = \u03a3 \u03b2\u1d62 \u2248 0.0065 (the \"delayed neutron fraction\").\n// This tiny fraction (~0.65%) is what makes reactors controllable!\n// Without it, the reactor period on prompt neutrons alone would be\n// milliseconds \u2014 far too fast for mechanical control rods.\n\nconst NUM_GROUPS: usize = 6;\nconst BETA: [f64; NUM_GROUPS] = [0.000215, 0.001424, 0.001274, 0.002568, 0.000748, 0.000273];\nconst LAMBDA: [f64; NUM_GROUPS] = [0.0124, 0.0305, 0.111, 0.301, 1.14, 3.01];\nconst BETA_TOTAL: f64 = 0.006502;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Material properties (pedagogically scaled) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n//\n// IMPORTANT: Physical thermal reactors have v \u2248 2.2 \u00d7 10\u2075 cm/s, giving a\n// prompt neutron generation time \u039b = 1/(v\u00b7\u03a3\u2090) \u2248 10\u207b\u2075\u201310\u207b\u2074 s.\n// At that speed, prompt dynamics are invisible at 30 fps.\n//\n// We scale v down to 50 cm/s so \u039b = 1/(50\u00b70.1) = 0.2 s, making prompt\n// responses visible over several frames.  The *relative* physics\n// (prompt vs delayed timescales, spatial diffusion) is preserved.\n\n/// Neutron velocity [cm/s].  Scaled for visualization (real: ~2.2e5).\nconst V_N: f64 = 50.0;\n\n/// Diffusion coefficient in fuel [cm].  (Stacey \u00a74.3)\nconst D_FUEL: f64 = 0.50;\n/// Macroscopic absorption cross-section in fuel [cm\u207b\u00b9].\nconst SIGMA_A_FUEL: f64 = 0.10;\n\n/// Diffusion coefficient in reflector [cm].\nconst D_REFL: f64 = 0.80;\n/// Macroscopic absorption cross-section in reflector [cm\u207b\u00b9].\nconst SIGMA_A_REFL: f64 = 0.02;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Reactivity schedule \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n//\n// The reactor sits slightly subcritical (k_eff \u2248 0.997, \u03c1 \u2248 \u22120.003).\n// Periodically, positive reactivity is inserted (simulating control rod\n// withdrawal), pushing k_eff to ~1.002 (delayed supercritical, \u03c1 < \u03b2).\n//\n// In this regime (Lamarsh \u00a77.3):\n//   \u2022 Prompt neutrons alone can't sustain a chain reaction.\n//   \u2022 Delayed neutrons make up the deficit \u2192 power rises on their\n//     timescale (~seconds), not the prompt timescale (~milliseconds).\n//   \u2022 When reactivity is removed, prompt flux drops immediately but\n//     accumulated precursors emit a slowly-decaying \"afterglow\".\n\n/// Base (subcritical) reactivity.  \u03c1 = (k\u22121)/k \u2248 \u22120.003.\nconst RHO_BASE: f64 = -0.003;\n/// Peak reactivity during rod withdrawal.  k \u2248 1.002, well below \u03b2.\nconst RHO_PEAK: f64 = 0.002;\n/// Period of the reactivity cycle [s].\nconst PULSE_PERIOD: f64 = 15.0;\n/// Ramp up/down duration [s] (control rod motion).\nconst RAMP_TIME: f64 = 0.5;\n/// Hold at peak reactivity [s].\nconst HOLD_TIME: f64 = 3.0;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 External neutron source \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// A subcritical reactor requires an external source to maintain non-zero\n// flux.  This models a startup source (e.g., Am-Be or \u00b2\u2075\u00b2Cf) at the\n// core center.\nconst SOURCE_STRENGTH: f64 = 5.0;\nconst SOURCE_RADIUS: f64 = 5.0;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Time integration \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n// Explicit Euler with sub-stepping for stability.\n//\n// CFL stability for 2D diffusion (Stacey \u00a75.5):\n//   dt < dx\u00b2 / (2 \u00b7 dim \u00b7 D \u00b7 v)  where dim = 2\n//      = 1.0 / (4 \u00b7 0.5 \u00b7 50) = 0.01 s\n//\n// 7 sub-steps at 30 fps \u2192 dt \u2248 0.0048 s.  Safe margin.\nconst SUB_STEPS: usize = 7;\nconst FPS: u32 = 30;\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Region classification \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq)]\nenum Region {\n    Fuel,       // Fissile material (UO\u2082 + moderator): has D, \u03a3\u2090, \u03bd\u03a3_f.\n    Reflector,  // Water reflector: has D, \u03a3\u2090, no fission.\n    Void,       // Outside reactor: zero-flux boundary.\n}\n\n// \u2500\u2500 Simulation state \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\nstruct ReactorSim {\n    phi: Vec<f64>,                       // Neutron flux \u03c6(x,y) [n/cm\u00b2/s]\n    buf: Vec<f64>,                       // Double-buffer for explicit Euler\n    precursors: [Vec<f64>; NUM_GROUPS],  // C\u1d62(x,y) for each delayed group\n    region: Vec<Region>,                 // Geometry mask\n    source: Vec<f64>,                    // External source S_ext(x,y)\n    time: f64,                           // Elapsed simulation time [s]\n}\n\nimpl ReactorSim {\n    #[inline]\n    fn idx(x: usize, y: usize) -> usize { y * N + x }\n\n    fn radius(x: usize, y: usize) -> f64 {\n        let dx = x as f64 - CENTER;\n        let dy = y as f64 - CENTER;\n        (dx * dx + dy * dy).sqrt()\n    }\n\n    /// Compute \u03c1(t) from the pulse schedule.\n    ///\n    /// Reactivity \u03c1 = (k\u22121)/k:\n    ///   \u03c1 < 0     \u2192 subcritical\n    ///   0 < \u03c1 < \u03b2 \u2192 delayed supercritical (prompt subcritical)\n    ///   \u03c1 = \u03b2     \u2192 prompt critical (dangerous threshold)\n    ///   \u03c1 > \u03b2     \u2192 prompt supercritical (very dangerous!)\n    fn reactivity(&self) -> f64 {\n        // Let the system reach subcritical equilibrium first.\n        if self.time < 4.0 {\n            return RHO_BASE;\n        }\n\n        // Periodic pulse: ramp up \u2192 hold \u2192 ramp down \u2192 wait.\n        let t = (self.time - 4.0) % PULSE_PERIOD;\n        let amp = if t < RAMP_TIME {\n            // Control rod withdrawing.\n            t / RAMP_TIME\n        } else if t < RAMP_TIME + HOLD_TIME {\n            // Rod out \u2014 peak reactivity.\n            1.0\n        } else if t < 2.0 * RAMP_TIME + HOLD_TIME {\n            // Rod inserting.\n            1.0 - (t - RAMP_TIME - HOLD_TIME) / RAMP_TIME\n        } else {\n            // Rod fully in \u2014 subcritical.  Delayed afterglow visible here.\n            0.0\n        };\n\n        RHO_BASE + (RHO_PEAK - RHO_BASE) * amp\n    }\n\n    /// Convert reactivity to \u03bd\u03a3_f (fission neutron production rate).\n    ///   \u03c1 = (k\u22121)/k  \u2192  k = 1/(1\u2212\u03c1)\n    ///   k_eff = \u03bd\u03a3_f / \u03a3\u2090  \u2192  \u03bd\u03a3_f = k \u00b7 \u03a3\u2090\n    fn nu_sigma_f(&self) -> f64 {\n        let k = 1.0 / (1.0 - self.reactivity());\n        k * SIGMA_A_FUEL\n    }\n\n    /// Map physics to RGB.\n    ///   Brightness \u221d log(flux).\n    ///   Hue = prompt/delayed ratio:\n    ///     Red/orange \u2192 prompt fission dominates.\n    ///     Blue/cyan  \u2192 delayed precursor decay dominates.\n    fn color(\n        intensity: f64,\n        prompt_frac: f64,\n        delayed_frac: f64,\n        region: Region,\n    ) -> (u8, u8, u8) {\n        match region {\n            Region::Void => (5, 5, 15),\n            Region::Reflector => {\n                let i = (intensity * 0.4).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n                ((i * 60.0) as u8, (i * 60.0) as u8, (i * 100.0) as u8)\n            }\n            Region::Fuel => {\n                let i = intensity.clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n                let r = (i * (0.25 + 0.75 * prompt_frac) * 255.0) as u8;\n                let g = (i * (0.10 + 0.50 * (prompt_frac * delayed_frac).sqrt()) * 255.0) as u8;\n                let b = (i * (0.12 + 0.88 * delayed_frac) * 255.0) as u8;\n                (r, g, b)\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nimpl Simulation for ReactorSim {\n    fn init() -> Self {\n        let ncells = N * N;\n        let mut region = vec![Region::Void; ncells];\n        let mut source = vec![0.0; ncells];\n        let mut phi = vec![0.0; ncells];\n\n        for y in 0..N {\n            for x in 0..N {\n                let r = Self::radius(x, y);\n                let c = Self::idx(x, y);\n\n                if r <= R_CORE {\n                    region[c] = Region::Fuel;\n                    // Gaussian seed so the initial subcritical state converges quickly.\n                    phi[c] = 0.1 * (-r * r / (2.0 * 40.0 * 40.0)).exp();\n                } else if r <= R_REFL {\n                    region[c] = Region::Reflector;\n                }\n\n                // Gaussian external source at center (startup source).\n                if r < SOURCE_RADIUS * 3.0 {\n                    source[c] = SOURCE_STRENGTH\n                        * (-r * r / (2.0 * SOURCE_RADIUS * SOURCE_RADIUS)).exp();\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Initialize precursors to steady-state equilibrium.\n        // At equilibrium, \u2202C\u1d62/\u2202t = 0 \u2192 C\u1d62 = \u03b2\u1d62\u00b7\u03bd\u03a3_f\u00b7\u03c6 / \u03bb\u1d62  (Keepin Eq. 4.12)\n        let k_init = 1.0 / (1.0 - RHO_BASE);\n        let nusf0 = k_init * SIGMA_A_FUEL;\n        let precursors = std::array::from_fn(|i| {\n            (0..ncells)\n                .map(|c| {\n                    if region[c] == Region::Fuel {\n                        BETA[i] * nusf0 * phi[c] / LAMBDA[i]\n                    } else {\n                        0.0\n                    }\n                })\n                .collect()\n        });\n\n        Self {\n            buf: phi.clone(),\n            phi,\n            precursors,\n            region,\n            source,\n            time: 0.0,\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn tick(&mut self) -> Canvas {\n        let dt = 1.0 / (FPS as f64 * SUB_STEPS as f64);\n\n        for _ in 0..SUB_STEPS {\n            let nu_sf = self.nu_sigma_f();\n\n            // \u2500\u2500 Step 1: Update neutron flux \u03c6(x,y) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n            //\n            // Discretized diffusion equation (explicit Euler):\n            //\n            //   \u03c6^(n+1) = \u03c6\u207f + v\u00b7dt \u00b7 [\n            //       D \u00b7 \u2207\u00b2\u03c6                    \u2190 spatial leakage\n            //     \u2212 \u03a3\u2090 \u00b7 \u03c6                     \u2190 absorption loss\n            //     + (1\u2212\u03b2) \u00b7 \u03bd\u03a3_f \u00b7 \u03c6           \u2190 prompt fission source\n            //     + \u03a3\u1d62 \u03bb\u1d62 C\u1d62                   \u2190 delayed neutron source\n            //     + S_ext                       \u2190 external source\n            //   ]\n            //\n            // The v factor comes from the LHS: (1/v)\u2202\u03c6/\u2202t = RHS  \u2192  \u2202\u03c6/\u2202t = v\u00b7RHS.\n\n            for y in 1..N - 1 {\n                for x in 1..N - 1 {\n                    let c = Self::idx(x, y);\n\n                    let (d, sigma_a, fissile) = match self.region[c] {\n                        Region::Fuel => (D_FUEL, SIGMA_A_FUEL, true),\n                        Region::Reflector => (D_REFL, SIGMA_A_REFL, false),\n                        Region::Void => {\n                            self.buf[c] = 0.0;\n                            continue;\n                        }\n                    };\n\n                    // 5-point discrete Laplacian:\n                    //   \u2207\u00b2\u03c6 \u2248 (\u03c6_E + \u03c6_W + \u03c6_N + \u03c6_S \u2212 4\u03c6_C) / \u0394x\u00b2\n                    // With \u0394x = 1, the denominator is implicit.\n                    let lap = self.phi[Self::idx(x + 1, y)]\n                        + self.phi[Self::idx(x - 1, y)]\n                        + self.phi[Self::idx(x, y + 1)]\n                        + self.phi[Self::idx(x, y - 1)]\n                        - 4.0 * self.phi[c];\n\n                    // Prompt fission source (only in fuel).\n                    // (1\u2212\u03b2)\u00b7\u03bd\u03a3_f\u00b7\u03c6 = fraction of fission neutrons emitted\n                    // \"promptly\" (within ~10\u207b\u00b9\u2074 s of fission event).\n                    let fission = if fissile {\n                        (1.0 - BETA_TOTAL) * nu_sf * self.phi[c]\n                    } else {\n                        0.0\n                    };\n\n                    // Delayed neutron source: \u03a3\u1d62 \u03bb\u1d62 C\u1d62(x,y).\n                    // Emitted by precursor nuclei (e.g. \u2078\u2077Br, \u00b9\u00b3\u2077I)\n                    // seconds to minutes after fission.\n                    let delayed: f64 = (0..NUM_GROUPS)\n                        .map(|i| LAMBDA[i] * self.precursors[i][c])\n                        .sum();\n\n                    let rhs = d * lap\n                        - sigma_a * self.phi[c]\n                        + fission\n                        + delayed\n                        + self.source[c];\n\n                    self.buf[c] = (self.phi[c] + V_N * dt * rhs).max(0.0);\n                }\n            }\n\n            std::mem::swap(&mut self.phi, &mut self.buf);\n\n            // \u2500\u2500 Step 2: Update precursor concentrations C\u1d62(x,y) \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n            //\n            // Each of 6 groups evolves independently (explicit Euler):\n            //\n            //   C\u1d62^(n+1) = C\u1d62\u207f + dt \u00b7 (\u03b2\u1d62 \u00b7 \u03bd\u03a3_f \u00b7 \u03c6  \u2212  \u03bb\u1d62 \u00b7 C\u1d62)\n            //                            \u2191 production       \u2191 decay\n            //\n            // Precursors have NO spatial diffusion \u2014 they are embedded in\n            // the solid fuel and \u03b2-decay in place, each emitting one neutron.\n\n            for i in 0..NUM_GROUPS {\n                for c in 0..N * N {\n                    if self.region[c] == Region::Fuel {\n                        let production = BETA[i] * nu_sf * self.phi[c];\n                        let decay = LAMBDA[i] * self.precursors[i][c];\n                        self.precursors[i][c] =\n                            (self.precursors[i][c] + dt * (production - decay)).max(0.0);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n\n            self.time += dt;\n        }\n\n        // \u2500\u2500 Render: map physics \u2192 color \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n        //\n        // Brightness = log-scaled neutron flux (wide dynamic range).\n        // Hue encodes the prompt-to-delayed source ratio:\n        //   Red/orange \u2192 prompt fission neutrons dominate.\n        //   Blue/cyan  \u2192 delayed neutrons from precursor decay dominate.\n\n        let nu_sf = self.nu_sigma_f();\n        let phi_max = self.phi.iter().copied().fold(0.0_f64, f64::max).max(1e-10);\n        let log_range = 20.0;\n\n        Canvas::from_fn(CANVAS_W, CANVAS_H, |px, py| {\n            // 400\u00d7400 canvas \u2192 200\u00d7200 grid (2\u00d7 upscale).\n            let x = (px as usize * N / CANVAS_W as usize).min(N - 1);\n            let y = (py as usize * N / CANVAS_H as usize).min(N - 1);\n            let c = Self::idx(x, y);\n\n            let reg = self.region[c];\n\n            // Logarithmic intensity for visual dynamic range.\n            let phi_n = self.phi[c] / phi_max;\n            let intensity = (1.0 + phi_n * log_range).ln() / (1.0 + log_range).ln();\n\n            // Decompose source into prompt vs delayed fractions.\n            let prompt = if reg == Region::Fuel {\n                (1.0 - BETA_TOTAL) * nu_sf * self.phi[c]\n            } else {\n                0.0\n            };\n            let delayed: f64 = (0..NUM_GROUPS)\n                .map(|i| LAMBDA[i] * self.precursors[i][c])\n                .sum();\n            let total = prompt + delayed + 1e-20;\n\n            Self::color(intensity, prompt / total, delayed / total, reg)\n        })\n    }\n\n    fn fps() -> u32 {\n        FPS\n    }\n}",
      "cargo_toml": null,
      "order": 0,
      "label": "Reactor Simulation",
      "cell_type": "Code"
    }
  ],
  "version": 1
}
